# ContextSpindle agent rules for Cursor

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/AGENT-PROTOCOL.md` before using project memory. The durable task ledger in `.contextspindle/tasks/` is authoritative; the bounded `.continuum/` retrieval cache can evict information.

At the start of work, use `contextspindle task context <id> <budget>` when an ID is known, otherwise inspect `task inbox` and `task search`. Create a task with a clear goal and completion criteria if needed. Record decisions, evidence, blockers, and the next action as the work changes. Before switching tasks, update the current task so another agent can resume it. Use `--expect-version` when coordinating concurrent writers. Verify and back up the ledger regularly. Do not install hooks, change IDE settings, or install a global CLI without a specific request.

The project-scoped `.mcp.json` exposes the same `contextspindle_task_*` interface. `contextspindle remember` and `recall` remain optional hints, not durable task storage.
